  "notes": "Very common in everyday conversation and written Japanese. The noun form {誤解|ごかい} is frequently used on its own.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {誤解|ごかい}を{招|まね}く: to invite misunderstanding\n- {誤解|ごかい}を{解|と}く: to clear up a misunderstanding\n- {誤解|ごかい}を{与|あた}える: to give a wrong impression\n- {誤解|ごかい}が{生|う}まれる: a misunderstanding arises\n- {誤解|ごかい}されやすい: easy to be misunderstood\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {勘違|かんちが}いする: to be mistaken, to get confused — more casual, often about factual mix-ups\n- {誤解|ごかい}する: to misunderstand — can involve deeper misinterpretation of meaning or intention",
